{
  "_comment": "Lease scheduler under other arrival rates and another workload mix, four slots, no host cache, seeds 42-44, each FIFO/lease pair back to back. In priority order: W1 at 1.15X (341 tasks, overload; 6 runs, ~1.8 h), W1 at 0.75X (223 tasks; 6 runs, ~1.5 h), then the synthetic mix at 1 task/s (200 tasks on 2,048-token slots, 70% single-step tasks, FIFO c = 4 as tuned in Phase 1; 6 runs, ~30 min). At 0.75X queues are short, so expect a smaller gain; in the mix only the agent tasks (30%) have a history to keep. Compare with: python -m analysis.paired results/phase2_lease_loads --baseline fifo_c5 --exclude 'mix_*'; and the mix with: python -m analysis.paired results/phase2_lease_loads --baseline fifo_c4 --exclude 'w1_*'",
